>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `add_split`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.add_split : thm -> simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds a local split looper applying `splitLib.SPLIT_TAC [th]`.

The name is `split name` (or `split_asm name` for an assumption rule), where
`name` is the theorem's database name, or its redex head constant's `thy$c`
when unnamed. Reusing the looper name replaces it. `ExclX "split:name"`
disables it for an invocation. This never registers or updates the persistent
`split` set.

### Failure

Fails if the theorem is not a split rule.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ext_bool_ss = simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss;
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.add_split (splitLib.type_split_of “:'a option”)
     ext_bool_ss;
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>> simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false} ss []
     ([], “P (case x of NONE => 0 | SOME n => n + 1) : bool”) c;
```

